/// A crate name shaped like one: lowercase, digits and hyphens, non-empty.
///
/// # Why the check stops here, and where the real one belongs
///
/// The obvious guard is "refuse a crate the workspace does not have", and it does NOT belong in this
/// crate. `plan.db` is the per-project store for ANY project — a CRM, a mobile app, a generated
/// site — and "the workspace" is meaningless for almost all of them. Teaching `plandb` to find a
/// repository root and parse its `Cargo.toml` would make every project pay for one project's model,
/// and would be wrong the moment a plan is opened outside a Rust checkout.
///
/// The existence check belongs where the roster is known, which is `bsc surface` — it already
/// derives the workspace members from the root manifest rather than a directory listing. Recorded
/// here so the gap reads as a decision rather than an oversight.
pub fn is_crate_name_shaped(name: &str) -> bool {
    !name.is_empty()
        && name.len() <= 64
        && name.chars().all(|c| c.is_ascii_lowercase() || c.is_ascii_digit() || c == '-')
}
